# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this, Git stored whatever line endings each contributor's machine
# produced. On Windows (core.autocrlf=true) that meant some files landed in
# history with CRLF and others with LF, and a branch that happened to
# normalize a file turned every line into a change — producing whole-file
# merge conflicts that look real but aren't (this bit PR #10's
# app/admin/orders/page.tsx).
#
# text=auto lets Git detect text vs binary; eol=lf fixes the in-repo form.
# Working copies on Windows still get CRLF on checkout via core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
